    "explanation": "To both parties: this case is escalated to a human reviewer under POL-GEN-26. No refund and no charge moves; the contested SGD 37.55 is held.\n\nWhat is established. Your trip ran 1.60 km off the recommended route — 22.9 km recorded against 21.3 km recommended on EV-TRIP-05011 — which is over the 1.0 km tolerance in POL-RD-22, so both advocates are right that the two within-tolerance rows of POL-RD-24 are unavailable. The vehicle left the PIE at the Eng Neo Avenue exit at 08:12:19 and rejoined at the Bukit Timah Road / CTE slip road at 08:22:49.\n\nJustification (POL-RD-23) — decided for the driver. EV-ADVIS-05011-01 is an ACCIDENT, an 'incident' in the policy's admissible traffic-justification types, on the Pan-Island Expressway towards Changi after the Adam Road exit, valid 07:44:37 to 08:54:37, which overlaps the 08:12:19–08:22:49 deviation. The rider's point that the artifact leaves intersects_route and justifies_reroute null is noted, but those fields are expressly left for the judge to determine from the advisory's road, direction and location against the trip: the departure point at Eng Neo is on the same PIE towards-Changi carriageway and west of the Adam Road exit, so the incident lies on the recommended route the driver was on. The reroute was traffic-justified, and the rider's contrary claim (row (d)) is rejected.\n\nWhat cannot be established is notice (POL-RD-21). The only carrier of whether the driver informed the rider before or at the point of deviation is EV-CHAT-05011, which is impaired at weight 0.4 for CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT: MSG-05011-003 carries a driver-device sent_at of 08:10:49 and a server delivered_at of 08:14:19, 210 s later and on the far side of the 08:12:19 deviation, and the admissibility note records that the device clock puts the notice before the deviation and the server clock after it. The driver's reading (that the 08:11:13 read receipt makes the earlier timeline the only consistent one) is one of the two the artifact holds; the record does not let me prefer it, because that contradiction is the very defect. EV-TRIP-05011's messages_during_trip block repeats the same messages and is not an independent carrier (POL-GEN-02(2)). An undecided limb supports neither row (a), which needs timely notice, nor row (b), which needs the rider to have been uninformed, so the case fits no row. The rider's 'ok can' at 08:14:39 has three agreeing timestamps, but it was sent after the vehicle had already left the PIE, so it cannot by itself make this a timely agreed deviation. The open question for the reviewer is therefore: was the driver's reroute message given to the rider before or at 08:12:19?\n\nConfidence. The notice fact is carried only by EV-CHAT-05011 at weight 0.4, so the cap under POL-GEN-02(2) is 0.4. POL-RD-25 and POL-GEN-22 require 0.80 for a 37.55 SGD dispute with no fraud flags (the 2 km limb is not in force, ai_ruling_max_deviation_applied false, as the driver correctly says), so the bar is not met and POL-GEN-26 requires escalation.\n\nOn the money, for completeness: had a refund been due it would be the excess distance fare only, 1.60 km × 0.72 SGD = 1.15 SGD without surge (EV-FARE-05011), as both sides accept. The full 37.55 SGD the rider asks for is not available on any row of POL-RD-24, and no lateness remedy exists in this version. No sum issues on an escalation. No referral applies — POL-NS-24, POL-NS-25 and POL-NS-22 have no application to a route deviation."
