    "explanation": "Both sides agree on the shape of the trip, and so do I. The platform's own recorded distances are 22.9 km actual against a 21.3 km recommended route (EV-TRIP-05011) — a deviation of 1.60 km, above the 1.0 km tolerance in POL-RD-22 — so the two \"within tolerance\" rows of the POL-RD-24 matrix are unavailable. The 19.158 km trace figure is not a distance measure; POL-RD-22 uses the trace only to show which route was taken and when.\n\nOn traffic justification (POL-RD-23) I find the reroute WAS justified, so I reject the rider's argument that it was not. EV-ADVIS-05011-01 is an LTA advisory of type ACCIDENT — an admissible \"incident\" type — on the Pan-Island Expressway towards Changi after the Adam Road exit, valid 07:44:37 to 08:54:37, a window that contains the whole deviation (08:12:19 to 08:22:49), and it records overlaps_trip_window as true. The artifact left intersects_route for the judge to determine. On its road (PIE, the recommended route's road), its direction (towards Changi, the vehicle's direction of travel) and its location (after Adam Road, on the stretch the vehicle would have continued along), it intersects the recommended route. The rider is right that the advisory orders no vehicle off the expressway, but POL-RD-23 requires only traffic data showing an incident on the recommended route segment at the trip time, which this is; and the null field is expressly marked for the judge, not a failed limb.\n\nThat leaves the notice limb of POL-RD-21, which decides between row (a) (informed and agreed — no refund) and row (b) (not informed — refund of the excess distance fare). That fact cannot be established on this record, and both advocates' timing claims fail on it. The notice is carried only by the chat log EV-CHAT-05011, which is IMPAIRED at weight 0.4 with issue code CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT: MSG-05011-003 carries a driver-device sent_at of 08:10:49 and a server delivered_at of 08:14:19 — 210 seconds apart, and on opposite sides of the 08:12:19 deviation event. I reject the driver's submission that the read receipt at 08:11:13 rescues the earlier reading: that timestamp sits before the server's own delivery time, so the three timestamps for that one message cannot all be true, and the conflict is real rather than a mere flag. I also reject the driver's submission that the trip record's message block (EV-TRIP-05011) independently carries the notice at weight 1.0: it repeats the same two messages from the same chat system and is a restatement of the same measurement, not a second carrier. The rider's \"he did not ask me before turning\" therefore cannot be resolved against the driver, and the driver's \"I messaged the passenger before I exit\" cannot be resolved for him; the account in the counterparty statement does not meet a limb POL-RD-21 ties to the chat log or a call recording.\n\nBecause the fact that decides between rows (a) and (b) rests on impaired evidence, POL-GEN-26 and POL-RD-24's \"fits no row\" rule send this to a human reviewer, and POL-RD-25 does the same: my confidence is capped by POL-GEN-02(2) at the 0.4 weight of the only artifact carrying the notice fact, below the 0.80 that POL-GEN-22 and POL-RD-25 require for a route-deviation ruling at this value. The contested 37.55 SGD sits in the 10.00–50.00 SGD band; neither profile carries a fraud flag (both read 0), so the 0.95 threshold does not apply.\n\nNo money issues. The disputed 37.55 SGD is held — not refunded, not kept. For completeness, I accept, as the driver does, that the only sum the matrix ever moves is the excess distance fare of 1.15 SGD (1.60 km at the 0.72 SGD per-km rate, without the 1.3 surge), which is what the rider now asks and what the driver correctly says no row can exceed; the full 37.55 SGD fare and the rider's lateness for her appointment are not remedies POL-RD-24 provides. But that figure cannot be paid at 0.4 confidence.\n\nOpen question for the human reviewer: from the driver's device clock the notice came before the deviation, from the platform's server clock it came after. The reviewer should determine which clock is right, and whether the rider's \"ok can\" at 08:14:39 was agreement to a notice already given or acquiescence to a reroute already under way.",
